🟡 **MODERATE:** For every user, the inner loop rescans the entire `orders` list, making this O(users * orders) instead of O(users + orders). On a warm report-generation path run repeatedly over the full collections, that quadratic cost is felt as latency growth as either side grows. Build an index once by grouping orders by `user_id` in a single pass, then look each user up in O(1) amortized:

```suggestion
def orders_for_users(users: list[dict], orders: list[dict]) -> dict:
    """Map each user id to their orders."""
    orders_by_user: dict = {}
    for order in orders:
        orders_by_user.setdefault(order["user_id"], []).append(order)
    return {user["id"]: orders_by_user.get(user["id"], []) for user in users}
```
